          "attribute": "question/problem",
          "value": "The maximum value of the quadratic form $Q(\\mathbf{x})= -x_1^2+2x_2^2+6x_3^2+4x_1x_2,$ when $\\| \\mathbf{x} \\| = 1,$ is equal to $6.$ Find a vector $\\mathbf{x}$ at which the maximum is attained.",
